# What #4471 contains

Ticket #4471 contains **412 unique reports** about dates landing on the wrong day.
The merged reports are two different problems, so the desk should track two tickets.

## The two problems

### Parser reads day-first dates as month-first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants using `booking-v2`,
and non-form reports from day-first tenants using `booking-v3`, can therefore have the
day and month flipped. This cause covers **379 reports**.

### booking-v3 shows the wrong hint

The `booking-v3` form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants. People follow that hint,
but the form reads the value using the tenant's day-first convention. This cause covers
**33 reports**.

## Evidence from the export

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The counts above use one report per report ID. The export has overlapping pages, so its
427 rows contain 15 duplicate rows. Five parser reports were read as a one-day move and
filed under the parser cause; they remain part of the parser count.

